{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, אָשַׁף","hw":"אָשַׁף","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">אָשַׁף</span></big>  (K <sup>§ 58 a</sup>) <strong>n.m. conjurer, enchanter (</strong>prob. Bab. loan-word; so BH <span dir=\"rtl\">אַשָּׁף</span><strong>)</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:10\" href=\"/Daniel.2.10\">Dn 2:10</a>; pl. abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">אָֽשְׁפִין</span> v <a data-ref=\"Daniel 2:27\" href=\"/Daniel.2.27\">27</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:11\" href=\"/Daniel.5.11\">5:11</a>, emph. <span dir=\"rtl\">אָֽשְׁפַיָּא</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:4\" href=\"/Daniel.4.4\">4:4</a>; <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:7\" href=\"/Daniel.5.7\">5:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 5:15\" href=\"/Daniel.5.15\">15</a>.","next":"BDB Aramaic, אֻשַּׁרְנָא","prev":"BDB Aramaic, אֻשֹּׁהִי"}